[2026-01-15T22:57:03.826698] PLAN PHASE:

Dependencies Analysis:
- construct_matrix: h[i][j] depends on h[i-1][j-1], h[i-1][j], h[i][j-1]
- True loop-carried dependency prevents row-wise or column-wise parallelization
- Anti-diagonal (wavefront) approach: cells on same diagonal are independent

Strategy Choice: WAVEFRONT PARALLELIZATION
- Process matrix by anti-diagonals (k = i+j)
- All cells on diagonal k only depend on diagonals k-1 and earlier
- Each diagonal can be computed in parallel
- Deterministic: fixed diagonal order, no race conditions

Patch Boundaries:
- Single file modification (construct_matrix method)
- Add Rayon dependency to Cargo.toml
- ~50 LOC change
- Public API unchanged

Alternatives Rejected:
1. Row-parallel: False - violates dependencies (h[i][j] needs h[i-1][j])
2. Column-parallel: False - violates dependencies (h[i][j] needs h[i][j-1])
3. Block-based tiling: Complex, harder to ensure determinism, more LOC
4. SIMD only: Limited by dependencies, not true parallelism

Chosen: Wavefront with Rayon bounded thread pool
